-- title:
--   Lemma 4 (Descent Property): sufficient decrease of $\mathcal V_k+\eta\epsilon_{k-1}^2$
-- statement:
--   Suppose that Assumptions 1, 2 and 3 hold and that the parameters are chosen as in (64) and (65). Let $\{(w^k;u^k;z^k;v^k)\}_{k\in\mathbb N}$ be a sequence generated by IALM satisfying the stopping criteria (32). Then for every $k\ge1$,
--   $$
--   (\mathcal V_k+\eta\epsilon_{k-1}^2)-(\mathcal V_{k+1}+\eta\epsilon_k^2)\ge\tau\|w^{k+1}-w^k\|^2,\qquad\tau:=\frac\mu4 .
--   $$
--   Here $\mathcal V_k=\mathcal V_{\rho,\beta}(w^k,u^k,z^k,v^{k-1})$ with $\beta=8c_2^2/\rho$.
--
--   This is the central estimate of the analysis: the merit sequence decreases by an amount controlling the primal step.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: a sequence generated by IALM, whose primal step is computed by 0/1-BALM (Algorithm 2) → every sequence satisfying (32a), (32b), (33) and vᵏ⁺¹ = wᵏ⁺¹ with positive tolerances; reason: every 0/1-BALM sequence satisfies these relations, and the proof in the paper uses only these relations
--   - generalization: Assumption 2 with γ := √θ_min(AAᵀ) > 0 → any γ > 0 with γ‖z‖ ≤ ‖Aᵀz‖ for every z; reason: the paper’s γ satisfies this inequality, so the printed statement is the instance γ = √θ_min(AAᵀ), and the proof uses Assumption 2 only through this inequality
--   - encoding: A ∈ ℝⁿˣᵖ and its transpose Aᵀ → a continuous linear map between Euclidean spaces and its adjoint; reason: the same objects in the standard bases
--   - encoding: k ∈ ℕ₊ → k : ℕ with 1 ≤ k; reason: the same index set
-- source:
--   Zhang & Xiu, Global Convergence of Inexact Augmented Lagrangian Method for Zero-One Composite Optimization, arXiv:2112.00440v1, Lemma 4, display (66), p.21

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ZeroOneIALM_Assumptions
import Definitions.Def_ZeroOneIALM_Parameters
import Definitions.Def_ZeroOneIALM_Run

namespace ZeroOneIALM

/-- Lemma 4 (Descent Property), Zhang & Xiu, arXiv:2112.00440v1, display (66), p.21: under
Assumptions 1, 2 and 3 and the parameter choices (64), (65), every IALM sequence satisfying (32) has
`(V_k + ηε²_{k-1}) - (V_{k+1} + ηε²_k) ≥ τ‖wᵏ⁺¹ - wᵏ‖²` for all `k ∈ ℕ₊`, where `τ := μ/4`. -/
theorem lemma_4 {p n : ℕ} {f : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin p) → ℝ}
    {A : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin p) →L[ℝ] EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)}
    {b : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)} {lam μ ρ lf γ η : ℝ} {ε : ℕ → ℝ}
    {w : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin p)} {u z : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)}
    {v : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin p)}
    (hlam : 0 < lam) (hμ : 0 < μ)
    (h1 : IsSmoothWith f lf) (h2 : IsRowRankConstant A γ) (h3 : IsBoundedBelow f)
    (hpar : IsParameterChoice μ lf γ ρ η ε)
    (hrun : IsIALMRun f A b lam μ ρ ε w u z v) (k : ℕ) (hk : 1 ≤ k) :
    (merit f A b lam ρ μ γ w u z v k + η * ε (k - 1) ^ 2) -
        (merit f A b lam ρ μ γ w u z v (k + 1) + η * ε k ^ 2) ≥
      μ / 4 * ‖w (k + 1) - w k‖ ^ 2 := by sorry

end ZeroOneIALM
